VERDICT: approve
{"verdict":"approve","summary":"The fix correctly narrows the clear span to exactly the redraw span (top..visible_rows), preserving terminal-scrolled content in the 0..top gap that the old unconditional 0..viewport.y clear would blank permanently. Tests cover the regression, the no-clamp baseline, and the overrun invariant, and the set_height caller's prior clear of old viewport rows is the only other region legitimately needing erasure.","concede":["I previously held needs-changes wanting stronger evidence that rows 0..top actually hold terminal-scrolled rather than stale content — re-reading set_height's shrink branch confirms old_y < new_y so rows 0..old_y were already above the old viewport (scrolled), and rows old_y..new_y are the caller-cleared vacated rows, so 0..top is a strict subset of the scrolled region and must not be touched."],"maintain":["The core logic is sound: start=max(naive_start,scrollback_committed), rows_to_draw=history_len-start, top=visible_rows-rows_to_draw, and clearing only top..visible_rows makes the clear span exactly equal the draw span, which is the correct invariant."],"findings":[]}
